-- ccc5-s117-01-to-117-012.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART III: section 117.01 (possession contrary to an order; failure to surrender) and the sub-heading
-- "Limitations on Access" (sections 117.0101 to 117.012). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the
-- Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING) or a core type. JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING otherwise.

§ `Part III continued -- offences, and limitations on access (ss 117.01 to 117.012)`

§§ `s 117.01 Possession contrary to order`

-- src:2464 | (4) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to the person as the result of an order made under subsection 113(1).
@ref s 117.01(4) (src:2464)
GIVEN `the person possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to the person as the result of an order made under subsection 113(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.01(4) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued as a result of an order under subsection 113(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to the person as the result of an order made under subsection 113(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2456 | 117.01 (1) Subject to subsection (4), every person commits an offence who possesses a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance while the person is prohibited from doing so by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament.
-- src:2464 | (4) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to the person as the result of an order made under subsection 113(1).
@ref s 117.01(1) (src:2456-2464)
GIVEN `s 2 firearm: the thing possessed is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2.1 the term has the meaning it has in subsection 84(1): the thing possessed is a cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition or prohibited ammunition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 explosive substance: the thing possessed is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is prohibited from possessing it by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.01(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 117.01(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply"
        IF ((`s 2 firearm: the thing possessed is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 2.1 the term has the meaning it has in subsection 84(1): the thing possessed is a cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition or prohibited ammunition` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 2 explosive substance: the thing possessed is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND `the person is prohibited from possessing it by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2458 | (2) Every person commits an offence who wilfully fails to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer any authorization, licence or registration certificate held by the person when the person is required to do so by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament.
@ref s 117.01(2) (src:2458)
GIVEN `the person wilfully fails to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer any authorization, licence or registration certificate held by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is required to do so by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.01(2) the person wilfully fails to surrender an authorization, licence or registration certificate when required by an order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person wilfully fails to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer any authorization, licence or registration certificate held by the person` AND `the person is required to do so by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2460 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)
@ref s 117.01(3) (src:2460)
GIVEN `the answer of s 117.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.01(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.01(3) the person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 117.01(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of s 117.01(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section reaches only the conduct its paragraphs describe

-- src:2460 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)
@ref s 117.01(3) (src:2460)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 117.01(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:2460 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)
-- src:2461 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
@ref s 117.01(3)(a) (src:2460-2461)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 117.01(3)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `by indictment`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no minimum
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine

-- src:2460 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)
-- src:2462 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 117.01(3)(b) (src:2460-2462)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 117.01(3)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the section states no penalty for the summary limb; section 787(1) supplies it

§§ `s 117.0101 Application for emergency limitations on access order`

-- src:2468 | 117.0101 (1) Any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an order under this section if the person believes on reasonable grounds that
-- src:2469 | (a) the person against whom the order is sought cohabits with, or is an associate of, another person who is prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things; and
-- src:2470 | (b) the other person would or might have access to any such thing that is in the possession of the person against whom the order is sought.
@ref s 117.0101(1) (src:2468-2470)
GIVEN `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the person against whom the order is sought cohabits with, or is an associate of, another person who is prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the other person would or might have access to any such thing that is in the possession of the person against whom the order is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(1) any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an emergency limitations on access order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the person against whom the order is sought cohabits with, or is an associate of, another person who is prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things` AND `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the other person would or might have access to any such thing that is in the possession of the person against whom the order is sought` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2472 | (2) The provincial court judge may hold the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) in private if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant.
@ref s 117.0101(2) (src:2472)
GIVEN `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(2) the provincial court judge may hold the hearing in private` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2474 | (3) If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist and that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person, the judge shall make an order in respect of the person against whom the order is sought, for a period not exceeding 30 days, as is specified in the order, beginning on the day on which the order is made, imposing any terms and conditions on the person’s use and possession of any thing referred to in subsection (1) that the judge considers appropriate.
@ref s 117.0101(3) (src:2474)
GIVEN `the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(3) the provincial court judge is bound to make an emergency limitations on access order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) has concluded` AND `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist` AND `the judge is satisfied that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist and that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person"


-- src:2474 | (3) If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist and that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person, the judge shall make an order in respect of the person against whom the order is sought, for a period not exceeding 30 days, as is specified in the order, beginning on the day on which the order is made, imposing any terms and conditions on the person’s use and possession of any thing referred to in subsection (1) that the judge considers appropriate.
@ref s 117.0101(3) (src:2474)
GIVEN period IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(3) the period of the order is not more than 30 days` MEANS
    IF period's years EQUALS 0 AND period's months EQUALS 0 AND period's days AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period not exceeding 30 days"

@ref s 117.0101(3) (src:2474)
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(3) the order begins on the day on which it is made` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the period begins` EQUALS `the day on which the order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "beginning on the day on which the order is made"

