-- src:2480 | (6) If a provincial court judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3) possesses, in a building, receptacle or place, any thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order, and that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess the thing, the judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search the building, receptacle or place and seize any such thing that is in the possession of the person.
-- src:2490 | (10) A provincial court judge may issue a warrant under subsection (6) or include in an order made under subsection (3) a requirement set out in subsection (9) only if they are satisfied that there is no other way to ensure that the terms and conditions of that order can reasonably be complied with.
@ref s 117.0101(6) (src:2480-2490)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3) possesses, in a building, receptacle or place, a thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.0101(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(6) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search and seize` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 117.0101(10)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if they are satisfied that there is no other way to ensure that the terms and conditions of that order can reasonably be complied with"
        IF `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3) possesses, in a building, receptacle or place, a thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order` AND `the judge is satisfied that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess the thing` AND (`the answer of s 117.0101(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2482 | (7) If, in respect of a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3), a peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess any thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order, the peace officer may — if the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (6) exist but, by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant — search for and seize any such thing that is in the possession of the person.
@ref s 117.0101(7) (src:2482)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the officer is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to an order made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, for the person to possess a thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (6) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 2 peace officer: the officer is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person is subject to an order made under subsection (3)` AND `the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, for the person to possess a thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order` AND `the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (6) exist` AND `by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2484 | (8) A peace officer who executes a warrant referred to in subsection (6) or who conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (7) shall immediately make a report to a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued, showing
@ref s 117.0101(8) (src:2484)
GIVEN `the peace officer executes a warrant referred to in subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(8) the peace officer is bound to make a report immediately to a justice having jurisdiction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the peace officer executes a warrant referred to in subsection (6)` OR `the peace officer conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (7)`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2484 | (8) A peace officer who executes a warrant referred to in subsection (6) or who conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (7) shall immediately make a report to a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued, showing
-- src:2485 | (a) in the case of an execution of a warrant, the things, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant; and
-- src:2486 | (b) in the case of a search conducted without a warrant, the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things, if any, seized.
@ref s 117.0101(8) (src:2484-2486)
GIVEN `the report is of an execution of a warrant and shows the things, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is of a search without a warrant and shows the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things, if any, seized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(8) the report shows what the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the report is of an execution of a warrant and shows the things, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant` OR `the report is of a search without a warrant and shows the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things, if any, seized`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2488 | (9) A provincial court judge who makes an order against a person under subsection (3) may, in the order, require the person to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer any thing the use or possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order that is in the possession of the person on the day on which the order is made, if the judge is satisfied by information on oath that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of any person for the person to possess the thing, and if the judge does so, they shall specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering the thing.
-- src:2490 | (10) A provincial court judge may issue a warrant under subsection (6) or include in an order made under subsection (3) a requirement set out in subsection (9) only if they are satisfied that there is no other way to ensure that the terms and conditions of that order can reasonably be complied with.
@ref s 117.0101(9) (src:2488-2490)
GIVEN `the judge makes an order against the person under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of any person for the person to possess the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is in the person's possession on the day on which the order is made and its use or possession is subject to terms and conditions under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.0101(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(9) the provincial court judge may require the person to surrender the things` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 117.0101(10)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if they are satisfied that there is no other way to ensure that the terms and conditions of that order can reasonably be complied with"
        IF `the judge makes an order against the person under subsection (3)` AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of any person for the person to possess the thing` AND `the thing is in the person's possession on the day on which the order is made and its use or possession is subject to terms and conditions under the order` AND (`the answer of s 117.0101(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2488 | (9) A provincial court judge who makes an order against a person under subsection (3) may, in the order, require the person to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer any thing the use or possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order that is in the possession of the person on the day on which the order is made, if the judge is satisfied by information on oath that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of any person for the person to possess the thing, and if the judge does so, they shall specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering the thing.
@ref s 117.0101(9) (src:2488)
GIVEN `the judge requires the person to surrender the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(9) the judge is bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering the thing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the judge requires the person to surrender the thing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the judge does so"

-- src:2492 | (11) A peace officer who has seized any thing under subsection (6) or (7), and a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer to whom any thing has been surrendered in accordance with subsection (9), may, before the expiry or revocation of the order made under subsection (3), on being issued a receipt for it, return the thing to the person from whom it was seized or who surrendered it, if the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer, as the case may be, has reasonable grounds to believe that the person will comply with the terms and conditions of the order as to the use and possession of the thing.
@ref s 117.0101(11) (src:2492)
GIVEN `the thing has been seized under subsection (6) or (7) by the peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing has been surrendered in accordance with subsection (9) to the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a receipt for it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person will comply with the terms and conditions of the order as to the use and possession of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order has not expired or been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a receipt for it is issued`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on being issued a receipt for it"
        IF (NOT `the order has not expired or been revoked`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the expiry or revocation of the order made under subsection (3)"
        IF (`the thing has been seized under subsection (6) or (7) by the peace officer` OR `the thing has been surrendered in accordance with subsection (9) to the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer`) AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person will comply with the terms and conditions of the order as to the use and possession of the thing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2494 | (12) Any things seized under subsection (6) or (7) from a person against whom an order has been made under subsection (3) and any things surrendered by the person in accordance with subsection (9) shall, unless already returned under subsection (11), be returned to the person
-- src:2495 | (a) if the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked, as soon as feasible after the day on which it is revoked; or
-- src:2496 | (b) in any other case, as soon as feasible after the end of the period specified in the order made against the person under subsection (3).
@ref s 117.0101(12) (src:2494-2496)
GIVEN `the things were seized under subsection (6) or (7) from a person against whom an order has been made under subsection (3), or surrendered by the person in accordance with subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period specified in the order made against the person under subsection (3) has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the things have already been returned under subsection (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0101(12) the things are to be returned to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the things have already been returned under subsection (11)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless already returned under subsection (11)"
        IF `the things were seized under subsection (6) or (7) from a person against whom an order has been made under subsection (3), or surrendered by the person in accordance with subsection (9)` AND (`the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked` OR `the period specified in the order made against the person under subsection (3) has ended`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 117.0102 Order denying access to information`

-- src:2498 | 117.0102 (1) If an order is made under subsection 117.0101(3), a provincial court judge may, on application by the person who applied for the order or on the judge’s own motion, if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person, make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, any or all of the following:
-- src:2499 | (a) any information relating to the order made under that subsection;
-- src:2500 | (b) any information relating to a warrant issued under subsection 117.0101(6);
-- src:2501 | (c) any information relating to a search and seizure conducted without a warrant under subsection 117.0101(7); and
-- src:2502 | (d) any information relating to the order made under this subsection.
@ref s 117.0102(1) (src:2498-2502)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection 117.0101(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the person who applied for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge acts on the judge's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the order made under subsection 117.0101(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to a warrant issued under subsection 117.0101(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to a search and seizure conducted without a warrant under subsection 117.0101(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the order made under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order is made under subsection 117.0101(3)` AND (`the application is made by the person who applied for the order` OR `the judge acts on the judge's own motion`) AND `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person` AND (`the information relates to the order made under subsection 117.0101(3)` OR `the information relates to a warrant issued under subsection 117.0101(6)` OR `the information relates to a search and seizure conducted without a warrant under subsection 117.0101(7)` OR `the information relates to the order made under this subsection`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)


-- src:2504 | (2) Unless an order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier, it expires on the day on which the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) expires or is revoked.
@ref s 117.0102(2) (src:2504)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) expires or is revoked` IS A DATE
      `the order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0102(2) the order made under subsection (1) expires on the day in question` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless an order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier"
        IF `the day in question` EQUALS `the day on which the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) expires or is revoked` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it expires on the day on which the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) expires or is revoked"

-- src:2506 | (3) Despite subsection (2), if, before the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 117.0104(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 117.011(1), an order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect on
-- src:2507 | (a) the date fixed under subsection 117.0104(1); or
-- src:2508 | (b) if the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) is revoked before that date, the day on which it is revoked.
@ref s 117.0102(3) (src:2506-2508)
GIVEN `a date is fixed under subsection 117.0104(1) before the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) expires or is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date fixed under subsection 117.0104(1)` IS A DATE
      `the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) is revoked before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which it is revoked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 117.0102(3) the day on which the order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a date is fixed under subsection 117.0104(1) before the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) expires or is revoked` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, before the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed"; subsection (2) governs
        IF `the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) is revoked before that date` THEN JUST `the day on which it is revoked`   -- (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST `the date fixed under subsection 117.0104(1)`   -- (a)

-- src:2510 | (4) If an order is made under subsection (1), all documents relating to, as the case may be, the order made under that subsection, the order made under subsection 117.0101(3), the warrant issued under subsection 117.0101(6) or, in the case of a search and seizure conducted without a warrant under subsection 117.0101(7), the report made under subsection 117.0101(8) shall — subject to any terms and conditions that the provincial court judge considers desirable in the circumstances, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, any term or condition concerning partial disclosure of a document, deletion of any information or the occurrence of a condition — be immediately placed in a packet and sealed by the judge, and the packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in any other place that the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with the terms and conditions specified in the order or as varied under subsection (5).
@ref s 117.0102(4) (src:2510)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document relates to the order made under subsection (1), the order made under subsection 117.0101(3), the warrant issued under subsection 117.0101(6) or the report made under subsection 117.0101(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0102(4) the documents are to be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order is made under subsection (1)` AND `the document relates to the order made under subsection (1), the order made under subsection 117.0101(3), the warrant issued under subsection 117.0101(6) or the report made under subsection 117.0101(8)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is made under subsection (1)"

-- src:2512 | (5) An application to revoke an order made under subsection (1) or vary any of its terms and conditions may be made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge.
@ref s 117.0102(5) (src:2512)
GIVEN `the application is to revoke an order made under subsection (1) or vary any of its terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to the provincial court judge who made the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to another provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0102(5) an application to revoke or vary the order may be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is to revoke an order made under subsection (1) or vary any of its terms and conditions` AND (`the application is made to the provincial court judge who made the order` OR `the application is made to another provincial court judge`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 117.0103 Order to delete identifying information`

-- src:2514 | 117.0103 (1) If an order is made under subsection 117.0101(3) or 117.0102(1), a provincial court judge may, on application by the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3) or on the judge’s own motion, if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person, make an order, subject to any terms and conditions that the judge considers desirable in the circumstances, directing that
-- src:2515 | (a) copies be made of any documents relating to the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) or 117.0102(1), as the case may be, including the order itself;
-- src:2516 | (b) any information that could identify the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3) or anyone known to the person be deleted from those copies; and
-- src:2517 | (c) the documents relating to the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) or 117.0102(1), as the case may be, including the order itself, to which the public has access or that are made available to or required to be served on any person are to be the edited copies referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 117.0103(1) (src:2514-2517)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection 117.0101(3) or 117.0102(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge acts on the judge's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0103(1) the provincial court judge may order that identifying information be deleted from copies of the documents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order is made under subsection 117.0101(3) or 117.0102(1)` AND (`the application is made by the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3)` OR `the judge acts on the judge's own motion`) AND `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2519 | (2) An order made under subsection (1) may be for any period — definite or indefinite — that the provincial court judge considers necessary to protect the security of the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3) or of anyone known to the person.
@ref s 117.0103(2) (src:2519)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers the period necessary to protect the security of the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3) or of anyone known to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0103(2) the order may be for any period, definite or indefinite, that the judge considers necessary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order is made under subsection (1)` AND `the judge considers the period necessary to protect the security of the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3) or of anyone known to the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2521 | (3) If an order is made under subsection (1), the originals of all documents that are the subject of the order shall — subject to any terms and conditions that the provincial court judge considers desirable in the circumstances — be immediately placed in a packet and sealed by the judge, and the packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in any other place that the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with the terms and conditions specified in the order or as varied under subsection (4).
@ref s 117.0103(3) (src:2521)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0103(3) the originals of the documents are to be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order is made under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is made under subsection (1)"

-- src:2523 | (4) An application to revoke an order made under subsection (1) or vary any of its terms and conditions may be made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge.
@ref s 117.0103(4) (src:2523)
GIVEN `the application is to revoke an order made under subsection (1) or vary any of its terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to the provincial court judge who made the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to another provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
