        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 117.0104 Order under subsection 117.011(5)`

-- src:2527 | 117.0104 (1) If a provincial court judge makes an order under subsection 117.0101(3), the judge may, on the judge’s own motion, fix a date for the hearing of an application made under subsection 117.011(1) and shall direct that notice of the hearing be given, in the manner that the judge may specify, to the person against whom an order under subsection 117.011(5) is sought.
@ref s 117.0104(1) (src:2527)
GIVEN `s 117.0101(3) an emergency limitations on access order has been made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0104(1) the provincial court judge may fix a date for the hearing of an application under subsection 117.011(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 117.0101(3) an emergency limitations on access order has been made` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2527 | 117.0104 (1) If a provincial court judge makes an order under subsection 117.0101(3), the judge may, on the judge’s own motion, fix a date for the hearing of an application made under subsection 117.011(1) and shall direct that notice of the hearing be given, in the manner that the judge may specify, to the person against whom an order under subsection 117.011(5) is sought.
@ref s 117.0104(1) (src:2527)
GIVEN `s 117.0101(3) an emergency limitations on access order has been made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the judge has fixed a date for the hearing of an application made under subsection 117.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0104(1) the provincial court judge is bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 117.0101(3) an emergency limitations on access order has been made` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the judge has fixed a date for the hearing of an application made under subsection 117.011(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a provincial court judge makes an order under subsection 117.0101(3)"

-- src:2529 | (2) For the purpose of this section,
-- src:2530 | (a) the application for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3) is deemed, except for the purpose of subsection 117.011(2), to be an application made under subsection 117.011(1); and
@ref s 117.0104(2)(a) (src:2529-2530)
GIVEN `the application is the application for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is the purpose of subsection 117.011(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0104(2)(a) the application for the order under subsection 117.0101(3) is deemed an application made under subsection 117.011(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the purpose is the purpose of subsection 117.011(2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for the purpose of subsection 117.011(2)"
        IF `the application is the application for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)


-- src:2529 | (2) For the purpose of this section,
-- src:2531 | (b) if a person other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer made the application for the order referred to in subsection 117.0101(3), the Attorney General of the province in which the application was made — or, if the application was made in a territory, the Attorney General of Canada — becomes the applicant, in their place, in the application made under subsection 117.011(1).
@ref s 117.0104(2)(b) (src:2529-2531)
GIVEN `the application was made by a person other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the application was made` IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`s 117.0104(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the application was made by a person other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer`
    THEN CONSIDER `where the application was made`
         WHEN Yukon THEN JUST `the Attorney General of Canada`
         WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN JUST `the Attorney General of Canada`
         WHEN Nunavut THEN JUST `the Attorney General of Canada`
         OTHERWISE JUST `the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a person other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer made the application"


-- src:2533 | (3) The date fixed for the hearing must be before the end of the period for which the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) is in force. However, a provincial court judge may, before or at any time during the hearing, on application by the applicant or the person against whom an order under subsection 117.011(5) is sought, adjourn the hearing.
@ref s 117.0104(3) (src:2533)
GIVEN `the date fixed for the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period for which the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) is in force ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0104(3) the date fixed for the hearing is before the end of the period of the order` MEANS
    IF `the date fixed for the hearing` LESS THAN `the day on which the period for which the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) is in force ends`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be before the end of the period for which the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) is in force"

-- src:2533 | (3) The date fixed for the hearing must be before the end of the period for which the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) is in force. However, a provincial court judge may, before or at any time during the hearing, on application by the applicant or the person against whom an order under subsection 117.011(5) is sought, adjourn the hearing.
@ref s 117.0104(3) (src:2533)
GIVEN `the application to adjourn is made by the applicant or by the person against whom an order under subsection 117.011(5) is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made before or at any time during the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0104(3) the provincial court judge may adjourn the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application to adjourn is made by the applicant or by the person against whom an order under subsection 117.011(5) is sought` AND `the application is made before or at any time during the hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before or at any time during the hearing, on application by the applicant or the person against whom an order under subsection 117.011(5) is sought"

-- src:2535 | (4) If the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 117.011(1), the provincial court judge shall, as soon as feasible but not later than 15 days before the date fixed under subsection (1), cause notice of that application and of that date to be served on that Attorney General.
@ref s 117.0104(4) (src:2535)
GIVEN `the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 117.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0104(4) the provincial court judge is bound to cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 117.011(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant"


-- src:2535 | (4) If the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 117.011(1), the provincial court judge shall, as soon as feasible but not later than 15 days before the date fixed under subsection (1), cause notice of that application and of that date to be served on that Attorney General.
@ref s 117.0104(4) (src:2535)
GIVEN `the date on which notice was served on the Attorney General` IS A DATE
      `the date fixed under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0104(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` MEANS
    IF `the date on which notice was served on the Attorney General` AT MOST `the date fixed under subsection (1)` MINUS 15
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 15 days before the date fixed"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The clock counts days from the day the date was fixed; the deadline is the 15th day before the date fixed.
-- "as soon as feasible" is a judgment with no number in the text, so only the outer limit is run (NOTES.md, fork register).
DECLARE `s 117.0104(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 117.0104(4) cause notice to be served on the Attorney General`

@ref s 117.0104(4) (src:2535)
GIVEN `the number of days from the day the date was fixed to the date fixed for the hearing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 117.0104(4) act`
`s 117.0104(4) the judge must cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` MEANS
    PARTY `a provincial court judge`
    MUST `s 117.0104(4) cause notice to be served on the Attorney General`
    WITHIN (`the number of days from the day the date was fixed to the date fixed for the hearing` MINUS 15)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a provincial court judge` BECAUSE "notice was not served on the Attorney General at least 15 days before the date fixed"

-- src:2537 | (5) If a provincial court judge revokes an order made under subsection 117.0101(3) against a person before the application for an order sought under subsection 117.011(5) against the person is heard, the judge shall cancel the hearing.
@ref s 117.0104(5) (src:2537)
GIVEN `the judge revokes an order made under subsection 117.0101(3) against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application for an order sought under subsection 117.011(5) against the person has not yet been heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.0104(5) the provincial court judge is bound to cancel the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the judge revokes an order made under subsection 117.0101(3) against the person` AND `the application for an order sought under subsection 117.011(5) against the person has not yet been heard` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a provincial court judge revokes an order made under subsection 117.0101(3)"

§§ `s 117.011 Application for order`

-- src:2539 | 117.011 (1) A peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order under this section where the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer believes on reasonable grounds that
-- src:2540 | (a) the person against whom the order is sought cohabits with, or is an associate of, another person who is prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things; and
-- src:2541 | (b) the other person would or might have access to any such thing that is in the possession of the person against whom the order is sought.
@ref s 117.011(1) (src:2539-2541)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the applicant is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the person against whom the order is sought cohabits with, or is an associate of, another person who is prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the other person would or might have access to any such thing that is in the possession of the person against whom the order is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.011(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order limiting access` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((`s 2 peace officer: the applicant is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the applicant is a firearms officer` OR `the applicant is a chief firearms officer`) AND `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the person against whom the order is sought cohabits with, or is an associate of, another person who is prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things` AND `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the other person would or might have access to any such thing that is in the possession of the person against whom the order is sought` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer believes on reasonable grounds that"

-- src:2543 | (2) On receipt of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge shall fix a date for the hearing of the application and direct that notice of the hearing be given, in such manner as the provincial court judge may specify, to the person against whom the order is sought.
@ref s 117.011(2) (src:2543)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 117.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.011(2) the provincial court judge is bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice be given to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an application has been made under subsection 117.011(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On receipt of an application made under subsection (1)"

-- src:2545 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), at the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge shall hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person against whom the order is sought.
