      `the judge proceeds ex parte under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.011(3) the provincial court judge is bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the hearing of an application made under subsection 117.011(1) is held` AND (NOT `the judge proceeds ex parte under subsection (4)`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2547 | (4) A provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine an application made under subsection (1) in the absence of the person against whom the order is sought in the same circumstances as those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant.
@ref s 117.011(4) (src:2547)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection 117.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person against whom the order is sought is absent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part XXVII the circumstances are those in which a summary conviction court may proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.011(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is made under subsection 117.011(1)` AND `the person against whom the order is sought is absent` AND (`Part XXVII the circumstances are those in which a summary conviction court may proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2549 | (5) Where, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist, the provincial court judge shall make an order in respect of the person against whom the order was sought imposing such terms and conditions on the person’s use and possession of anything referred to in subsection (1) as the provincial court judge considers appropriate.
@ref s 117.011(5) (src:2549)
GIVEN `the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
